# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SSIP — GOVERNANCE-SAFE ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This file defines the governance-safe environment configuration contract
# for the Student Success Intelligence Platform (SSIP).
#
# Governance architecture:
#   * Execution mode governs all platform behavior — not feature flags
#   * Config V2 governs orchestration thresholds — not environment variables
#   * Providers are platform_supplementary — GHL, Synthflow, and AI are
#     delivery vehicles, not authority boundaries
#   * SHADOW is the mandatory default operational tier — not a debug toggle
#   * Attribution continuity is mandatory on every record (INV-5)
#   * SQL Server is a read-only authoritative source (FAD-5); no write grants
#   * Three-schema service account model applies in all environments
#
# What this file does NOT configure:
#   * Retry thresholds — governed by Config V2 Group A
#     (outreach_max_retry_attempts, outreach_retry_interval_hours)
#   * Concurrency limits — governed by Config V2 Group A
#     (orchestration_concurrency_limit)
#   * Channel progression rules — governed by Config V2
#   * Feature flags — governance invariants are universal;
#     no flag may suppress INV-1–INV-7 or FAD-1–FAD-6
#   * MVP/STANDARD/PRODUCTION tier behavior — deprecated;
#     governance invariants apply without tier relaxation
#
# Canonical references:
#   runtime/system_loop.md       — six canonical execution modes, AP-RT7
#   spec/01_requirements.md      — governance model, FAD-1–FAD-6
#   spec/03_state_transition_rules.md — INV-1–INV-7
#   failure/failure_playbook.md  — AP-FP1–AP-FP8, Config V2 threshold governance
#   execution/build_phases.md    — Phase 1–12 certification-gated rollout
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── EXECUTION MODE GOVERNANCE ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# EXECUTION_MODE governs all platform behavior. Valid values:
#
#   SHADOW  — mandatory default operational tier. All outbound provider
#             dispatch is suppressed (outbound_suppressed = true; no HTTP).
#             Orchestration evaluation runs fully. All outputs carry
#             governance_scope = SHADOW_ONLY. SHADOW mode is not a debug
#             toggle — it is a governance-required pre-production state.
#             (runtime/system_loop.md §3.2)
#
#   LIVE    — governed provider delegation. Outbound dispatch authorized
#             when ProviderOrchestrationAssessment.governance_scope = AUTHORIZED.
#             Requires: activation_record_present = true in Config Version
#             Registry, Governance Administrator authorization, explicit
#             acknowledgement, and Phase 12 certification completion.
#             LIVE must not be set without GA sign-off (AP-RT7).
#             (runtime/system_loop.md §3.1; execution/build_phases.md §12)
#
#   REPLAY  — historical orchestration simulation. All outputs carry
#             execution_type = replay, governance_scope = REPLAY_ONLY,
#             live_effects_produced = 0. Replay always uses
#             historical_config_version_id — never the current ACTIVE config.
#             Non-zero live_effects_produced in REPLAY mode is a CRITICAL
#             governance alert (INV-4, AP-RT2).
#             (runtime/system_loop.md §3.3)
#
# All six canonical modes (LIVE, SHADOW, REPLAY, REGENERATION, DEGRADED,
# MAINTENANCE) are defined in runtime/system_loop.md §3.
#
# SHADOW → LIVE transition governance:
#   Automated services may NOT trigger this transition. Transition requires
#   GA authorization + activation_record_present = true + explicit
#   acknowledgement checkbox (AP-RT7, runtime/system_loop.md §3.5).
#
EXECUTION_MODE=SHADOW


# ── POSTGRESQL — PLATFORM SYSTEM OF RECORD ────────────────────────────────
#
# PostgreSQL is the exclusively platform-owned intelligence, operations,
# and reporting database. Three-schema architecture applies:
#
#   public              — operational state; app_service_user has
#                         SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE on mutable tables; INSERT-only
#                         on append-only tables (student_timeline_events,
#                         state_transition_log, outreach_history,
#                         processed_events)
#
#   warehouse           — governed historical intelligence; finalization_service_user
#                         has INSERT-only access; FINALIZED snapshots and
#                         REPORT_PUBLISHED reports are permanently immutable
#                         (INV-1, INV-6, FAD-1, FAD-2)
#
#   compliance_audit    — compliance and deletion pathway records;
#                         compliance_pathway_user has INSERT-only access;
#                         no external system may read or write directly
#                         (FAD-6, spec/09_security_privacy.md)
#
# The database URL is typically set by Docker Compose. Do not hardcode
# production credentials in this file.
#
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://ssip:ssip@localhost:5432/ssip


# ── SQL SERVER — READ-ONLY AUTHORITATIVE SOURCE ───────────────────────────
#
# SQL Server is origin_authority = sql_server_authoritative. It is the
# source of record for student academic and operational data.
#
# Governance boundary (FAD-5):
#   * Platform services have SELECT-only access — no write grants provisioned
#   * Any write attempt produces ArchitecturalViolation
#   * SQL Server data wins on field conflicts (origin_authority precedence)
#   * All ingested records carry origin_source = mirrored_sql_server and
#     is_authoritative = true (spec/05_external_integrations.md §2.3)
#
# The sync service reads from SQL Server and UPSERTs into
# public.student_trigger_data with full attribution fields.
# SQL Server itself is never written to by any platform service.
#
MSSQL_HOST=
MSSQL_PORT=1433
MSSQL_USER=
MSSQL_PASS=
MSSQL_DATABASE=


# ── GHL (GoHighLevel) — PLATFORM SUPPLEMENTARY PROVIDER ──────────────────
#
# GHL is origin_authority = platform_supplementary. It is a delivery
# vehicle for governed outreach intents — not an authority boundary.
#
# SHADOW mode behavior:
#   All outbound GHL dispatch is suppressed (outbound_suppressed = true).
#   No HTTP calls are made. Orchestration intents are evaluated and logged
#   with governance_scope = SHADOW_ONLY. GHL credentials may be left empty
#   in SHADOW mode — the runtime suppresses dispatch before credential use.
#
# LIVE mode behavior:
#   GHL dispatch is authorized only when ProviderOrchestrationAssessment
#   carries governance_scope = AUTHORIZED. No runtime loop calls GHL
#   directly — all dispatch is delegated to the GHL orchestration service
#   (AP-RT1, runtime/system_loop.md §2.4).
#
# REPLAY mode behavior:
#   All GHL interactions return historical records only. No live GHL API
#   calls. All outputs carry execution_type = replay (runtime/system_loop.md §3.3).
#
GHL_API_KEY=
GHL_BASE_URL=https://rest.gohighlevel.com
GHL_LOCATION_ID=


# ── SYNTHFLOW — PLATFORM SUPPLEMENTARY PROVIDER ───────────────────────────
#
# Synthflow is origin_authority = platform_supplementary. It is a voice
# call delivery vehicle — not an authority boundary.
#
# SHADOW mode behavior:
#   All outbound Synthflow dispatch is suppressed. No HTTP calls are made.
#   Credentials may be left empty in SHADOW mode.
#
# LIVE mode behavior:
#   Synthflow dispatch is authorized only under governed intent delegation
#   with governance_scope = AUTHORIZED.
#
# REPLAY mode behavior:
#   All Synthflow interactions return historical records only.
#   No live Synthflow API calls. All outputs carry execution_type = replay.
#
SYNTHFLOW_API_KEY=
SYNTHFLOW_PHONE_NUMBER=


# ── ANTHROPIC — AI ADVISORY PROVIDER ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# Anthropic Claude is the AI advisory provider. AI outputs are advisory
# only — labeled ai_governance_tier and never used as sole authority for
# LIVE escalation decisions (AP-AI11, spec/01_requirements.md §3.4).
#
# AI governance boundaries:
#   * FINALIZED_COPY AI narratives are deep-copied at FINALIZED time and
#     permanently immutable (FAD-1, INV-6; allows_update = false)
#   * AI narratives in warehouse.snapshot_ai_narratives are INSERT-only
#     after allows_update = false is set
#   * In REPLAY mode: live AI inference is suppressed; FINALIZED_COPY is
#     sourced exclusively from warehouse.snapshot_ai_narratives (FAD-2)
#   * In REGENERATION mode: no live AI inference; warehouse-sourced only
#   * In SHADOW mode: AI inference runs; outputs tagged outcome = shadow_only
#
# SHADOW mode behavior:
#   AI advisory generation runs and is logged. Outputs carry
#   execution_mode = SHADOW and are not used for LIVE escalation.
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY may be left empty to suppress AI advisory calls
#   entirely in SHADOW mode; the platform degrades gracefully with
#   ai_governance_tier = UNAVAILABLE (failure/llm_failures.md).
#
# Model selection:
#   Default: claude-sonnet-4-6 (current production-tier advisory model).
#   Model version is attributed in all AI narrative records as
#   fingerprint_ai_model_version for lineage reproducibility.
#   Model changes require a new Config Version activation (FAD-3).
#
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6


# ── SCHEDULER GOVERNANCE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# APScheduler coordinates daily orchestration cycle timing. Scheduler
# behavior is governed by runtime/scheduler_design.md.
#
# What scheduler timing variables configure:
#   SCHEDULER_HOUR, SCHEDULER_MINUTE, SCHEDULER_TIMEZONE define the
#   wall-clock trigger for daily orchestration cycle initiation.
#
# What scheduler timing variables do NOT configure:
#   * Retry cadences — governed by Config V2 Group A
#     (outreach_retry_interval_hours)
#   * Retry attempt ceilings — governed by Config V2 Group A
#     (outreach_max_retry_attempts)
#   * Concurrency limits — governed by Config V2 Group A
#     (orchestration_concurrency_limit)
#   * Recovery cycle timing — governed by Config V2
#     (runtime/scheduler_design.md §4)
#
# No hardcoded orchestration thresholds are permitted in environment
# configuration. All operational thresholds resolve dynamically from
# the ACTIVE Config Version at orchestration cycle start (INV-7).
#
# Attribution: every scheduler-triggered cycle emits a correlation_id
# and carries execution_mode, execution_type, and config_version_id on
# all records produced during that cycle (INV-5).
#
SCHEDULER_HOUR=18
SCHEDULER_MINUTE=0
SCHEDULER_TIMEZONE=America/Chicago


# ── OBSERVABILITY AND ATTRIBUTION GOVERNANCE ──────────────────────────────
#
# Attribution continuity is mandatory on every record (INV-5).
# The following attribution fields must be present on all governance-
# sensitive records — null values surface ATTRIBUTION_INCOMPLETE:
#
#   correlation_id      — UUID v4; generated at orchestration cycle entry;
#                         propagates through all service calls, log entries,
#                         and database writes within the cycle
#   execution_mode      — SHADOW | LIVE | REPLAY | REGENERATION | DEGRADED |
#                         MAINTENANCE; set from EXECUTION_MODE at cycle start
#   execution_type      — standard | replay; replay records are permanently
#                         distinguishable from LIVE records
#   config_version_id   — FK to the ACTIVE Config Version at cycle start;
#                         replay uses historical_config_version_id
#
# Two-category telemetry model (spec/06_observability_operations.md §1.2):
#   Operational telemetry  — real-time monitoring; stdout JSON log stream
#   Governance telemetry   — audit, lineage, compliance; append-only DB tables
#
# Both categories are required. Governance telemetry is authoritative in
# any investigation. Operational telemetry is contextual. Neither replaces
# the other.
#
# No additional environment variables are required for observability.
# Log schema, correlation_id propagation, and governance transition
# entries are implemented in the application layer per
# spec/06_observability_operations.md §3.


# ── CERTIFICATION-GATED ROLLOUT ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The platform advances to LIVE only after Phase 12 certification.
# No automated service may trigger SHADOW → LIVE transition (AP-RT7).
#
# Certification gates (execution/build_phases.md; evolution/versioning_strategy.md §7):
#
#   SHADOW containment       — SVL-1–SVL-3       tests/test_shadow_safety.py  Phase 6
#   Replay isolation         — ROS-1–2, INV-4    tests/test_shadow_safety.py  Phase 7
#   Immutable-lineage        — INV-1, INV-6      tests/test_shadow_safety.py  Phase 8
#   Attribution continuity   — INV-5             tests/test_shadow_safety.py  Phase 8
#   Observability            — ROG-1–7           tests/test_dashboard.py      Phase 9
#   Resilience               — AP-FP1–AP-FP8     failure/failure_playbook.md  Phase 10
#   Synchronization          — SQL Server RO     tests/test_sync.py           Phase 5
#   Config V2 governance     — INV-2, INV-7      tests/test_shadow_safety.py  Phase 4
#   Priority engine          — work queue        tests/test_work_queue.py     Phase 5
#   SHADOW → LIVE transition — CV2-4, AP-RT7     tests/test_shadow_safety.py  Phase 12
#
# Deployment maturity classification (evolution/versioning_strategy.md §6.2):
#
#   DEVELOPMENT          — EXECUTION_MODE=SHADOW; no certification required
#   STAGING              — EXECUTION_MODE=SHADOW; Phases 1–8 validated
#   PRE-PRODUCTION       — EXECUTION_MODE=SHADOW; Phases 1–11 complete
#   PRODUCTION (SHADOW)  — EXECUTION_MODE=SHADOW; Phase 12 readiness; GA review
#   PRODUCTION (LIVE)    — EXECUTION_MODE=LIVE;   Phase 12 complete;
#                          activation_record_present = true;
#                          GA authorization + acknowledgement (AP-RT7)
#
# Governance architecture never downgrades. INV-1–INV-7 and FAD-1–FAD-6
# are permanently deployed across all certification stages.
